invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_avx512.h
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_avx512.h's gcm_use_avx512 answers 1 whatever the key's session
  stated, so every AES-GCM key of an x86-64 host object that runs on the
  instructions runs the 512-bit kernel, and dies of SIGILL on a CPU without
  AVX-512. Every vector passes on a CPU with it. The script compiles gcm.c
  for x86-64 and requires its object to call gcm_hw.c's and gcm_vaes.c's
  entries, the paths a key without the bit runs, which the compiler then
  drops as unreachable.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512) != 0 && (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) != 0 &&
           (cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 1;
